On Windows, `which` tries each `PATHEXT` item twice: as written and in lower case. On a file system
that ignores case (NTFS by default), both `tool.CMD` and `tool.cmd` find the same file, so with
`all: true`, `findExecutable` and `findExecutableSync` returned every match twice. A lowercase item
like `.cmd` gave the same path twice even where case matters. Now only the first case variant that
exists is a match. The latest release (7.0.0) still has this bug.

